.TH SDL_ShowSimpleMessageBox 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ShowSimpleMessageBox \- Display a simple modal message box.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_messagebox.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_ShowSimpleMessageBox(SDL_MessageBoxFlags flags, const char *title, const char *message, SDL_Window *window);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If your needs aren\(aqt complex, this function is preferred over
.BR SDL_ShowMessageBox \[char46]
.PP
.BR flags
may be any of the following:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_MESSAGEBOX_ERROR :
error dialog
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_MESSAGEBOX_WARNING :
warning dialog
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_MESSAGEBOX_INFORMATION :
informational dialog
.PP
This function should be called on the thread that created the parent window, or on the main thread if the messagebox has no parent\[char46] It will block execution of that thread until the user clicks a button or closes the messagebox\[char46]
.PP
This function may be called at any time, even before
.BR SDL_Init ()\[char46]
This makes it useful for reporting errors like a failure to create a renderer or OpenGL context\[char46]
.PP
On X11, SDL rolls its own dialog box with X11 primitives instead of a formal toolkit like GTK+ or Qt\[char46]
.PP
Note that if
.BR SDL_Init ()
would fail because there isn\(aqt any available video target, this function is likely to fail for the same reasons\[char46] If this is a concern, check the return value from this function and fall back to writing to stderr if you can\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I flags
an
.BR SDL_MessageBoxFlags
value\[char46]
.TP
.I title
UTF-8 title text\[char46]
.TP
.I message
UTF-8 message text\[char46]
.TP
.I window
the parent window, or NULL for no parent\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_ShowMessageBox (3)
